REQ-ARC-WMTE-6660. Three A/Bs produced no readable firing evidence and
the offline replay (25/25 would-have-fired) could not recover the ARM
choice because per-window eligibility bits were never recorded. The
supervisor now exists on EVERY run: env=1 applies redirects as before
(mode: applied); anything else is SHADOW — observe() runs identically
and redirects land in the receipt as would_have_redirects /
would_have_arm_outcomes, never applied. Keys disambiguate BY NAME;
enabled keeps its historical was-anything-applied meaning; shadow rows
rename resolved_by_levelup to levelup_followed_without_redirect (the
CONTROL outcome there). Supervision is fail-open for the scored path,
direction stated, visible via observe_errors.

Zero scored-path change PROVEN: the shadow seam test pins bias
identity, diversity flag and the induction latch untouched; its
mutation (shadow gate removed) goes RED on the real applied effect.
Four mutations RED->GREEN; 28 supervisor + 18 downstream tests pass;
exp6524 preserved (shadow receipts carry no redirects key).

